{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/778078-can-a-caern-go-dormant","id":778078,"title":"Can a Caern go Dormant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-01T20:29:43-08:00","id":778078,"title":"Can a Caern go Dormant?","content":"Is it possible for a dormant Caern to Survive only to once rediscovered be revived...<br /> <br /> Was thinking maybe one captured by witchhunters where a church maybe a monastary was built over it, only for the protaganists to annihilate the church and reclaim the caern... creating a nice backdrop, on the whole &quot;Good guy/bad guy&quot; thing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T00:05:46-08:00","id":778150,"title":"","content":"Maybe.... In the rules I think a caern dies if there isn't Gnosis sacrificed during a moot rite every month (5 per level iirc). But there are tales of lost caerns found very so often. 1st Edition makes it a common rite of passage for Black Furies to find lost caerns, which is probably bullshit viewed from revised Edition standpoint.<br /> <br /> But my opinion is, yes, it could be possible. Especially if in your case the monks or nuns have been doing spiritual stuff there every day, possibly keeping the caern spiritually active in some way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T00:08:42-08:00","id":778152,"title":"","content":"I would imagine the spirit would lapse into slumber since its gnosis pool has run out, isn't there a rite of caern reawakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T00:21:33-08:00","id":778157,"title":"","content":"Yes, Caerns go dormant. And Why would you annihilate the Church? You can just co-opt it and still use it as a Caern, as long as the witch-hunters didn't destroy it, which is more likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T08:26:40-08:00","id":778336,"title":"","content":"Yes they can. There are numerous instances of this happening in previous books. The Outcasts book says that the Skin Dancers have two such caerns, one they have managed to reopen and another (previous Nuwisha caern) that they haven't. The Australia books that while many of the Bunyip's caerns were taken over by invading tribes there are still some that they haven't been able to unlock once they went dormant.<br /> <br /> I have to agree with Cogliostro, makes no sense to destroy the Church, Glasswalkers were known in the dark ages for being part of the church. I could see several tribes taking advantage of the build that is already there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T09:01:28-08:00","id":778355,"title":"","content":"Really almost any tribe could use the church caern.<br /> Black Furies-purchase the building and by day run women empowerment seminars, counselling on parenting, a new nun order.<br /> Bone Gnawers-a bit difficult to pull off with no or few resources but soup kitchen, homeless shelter, or even a specialized pantry/ clothes bank<br /> Children of Gaia-purchase and repurpose as the Church of the Divine.<br /> Fianna-purchase turn it into a pub. <br /> Get of Fenris-purchase after slaughtering the hunters and turn it into apartments.<br /> Glass Walkers- any of the above.<br /> Silver Fangs- purchase the land and create a park by buying and razing the neighborhood or if historical preserve and turn into a museum.<br /> Silent Striders- again a bit problematic but hey might make for an interesting Bed and Breakfast.<br /> Shadow Lords- nightclub, yes nightclub there has to be away you can turn this into a trap for vampires and mages and pesky Silver Fangs.<br /> Uktena-again a bit problematic.<br /> Wendigo- not feeling it caern or no caern.<br /> White Howlers- non historical timeline pick a reason based on how the tribe survived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T09:31:12-08:00","id":778393,"title":"","content":"Killing the hunters is one thing, but assuming this place isn't some monastery out in the middle of nowhere, you don't just get access to a building by killing the current inhabitants. That church is owned by someone, maybe an individual, maybe the Catholic church, maybe they were renting the space from a land holder. If the werewolves raze or squat in the church after killing all the hunters, that is going to get really awkward when the police/taxmen/deed owners start asking questions. Holding onto the caern long term should require buying/ legally attaining the church to protect the Veil. Kinfolk proxies, gifts and quality forgery work are gonna come in quite handy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T09:59:14-08:00","id":778416,"title":"","content":"so this works better for a historical game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T12:29:50-08:00","id":778520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/778078-can-a-caern-go-dormant?p=778416#post778416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so this works better for a historical game?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's the same. Just easier with less paperwork and communication to fuck with your cunning plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T20:23:30-08:00","id":778781,"title":"","content":"Naw man, level that place. Claim it as an &quot;act of god&quot;. What's the worst that could happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T07:01:50-08:00","id":778976,"title":"","content":"Churches run into financial trouble all of the time. Quite a few of my examples are inspired by real places in my city. Another source for a Caern in a city setting or at least possible is an old school. I could totally buy a caern of survival in an old school.<br /> <br /> But yes buying the land is a much better option than slaughtering the hunters and squatting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T08:48:47-08:00","id":779032,"title":"","content":"Depends on the area where you play. In Germany church communities are only semi-independent. Churches are basically state wide organizations and independent communities of smaller religions are rare. And while the larger churches have their own financial challenges they are still the largest private land owner in all of Germany.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}